{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791564954,"nonce":"JjeHQxC4jcpUFY7e3Rfh7+tGKrM=","message":"Landed in b36d3cd118339d602aceb70f9fb295e34e32f33b. Scopes::prune_unused_functions marks `local function` variables that are never assigned, carry no attribute, and are named only inside functions that are pruned or nested in one (greatest fixed point over body-span nesting). Lowering skips their statements. Called from program() for the main file and required files only when no file reaches the debug library, and from loaded_types for a `load`ed chunk only when neither the program's remembered debug mode nor the chunk reaches it. Compile-time errors in pruned bodies still fire: parse.rs checks goto/const/break before lowering. `local f = function ... end` is not pruned (the statement shape is not recorded in scopes); scope flags such as `captured` still count uses inside pruned bodies.\n\nFixture (100 x `local function unused_N(x) return x + 1 end` + print): own functions 201 -\u003e 1, declarations 284 -\u003e 79, functions kept 358 -\u003e 136, identical to the empty chunk. Mac, release, LLVM unselected, 9 interleaved rounds under load average about 25: wall median 60.57 -\u003e 20.51 ms (empty 21.67 -\u003e 23.40, Lua nbody 251.25 -\u003e 244.38: noise). closures/unused_local_functions.lua: main own functions 33 -\u003e 17; its loaded chunk 85 -\u003e 83 declarations.\n\nValidation: new conformance cases closures/unused_local_functions and debug/getlocal_unused_functions pinned against lua 5.4.9; Lua conformance 46/46, capi 3/3, official_suite 4/4; scope unit tests (transitive, nested, past-nested use, shadowed, assigned); all 17 Lua benchmark outputs equal lua5.4's. NUC frozen-binary timing not run yet (NUC busy with another session's build).","files":null}]}